// Durations, time points, the system and steady clocks, whose now() is in featheros_cxx, the
// civil calendar's day, month, year, weekday and dates, and hh_mm_ss, so the kernel can use all
// but the clocks. Formatting (__chrono_format) is for programs only, as <format> is. Time zones,
// the rest of the calendar (weekday_indexed, year_month_day_last, ...) and the C++20 clocks
// (utc_clock, file_clock, ...) are left out, as are the floating-point literals (1.5s): they take
// a long double, which AArch64 cannot convert at run time without a compiler runtime.

